---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Facturazaz | Carlos Menco Guardo" mainClass="main-content main-content--project-detail" activePage="facturazaz" pageScripts={["/js/project-scroll-gradient.js"]}>
  <div class="content--sidebar">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-img-wrapper">
        <img src="/imgs/facturazaz-thumb.svg" alt="Facturazaz application preview" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="s1">
      <span class="project-detail-year">2026</span>
      <h5 class="project-detail-title">Facturazaz</h5>
      <p class="project-detail-description">A SaaS invoicing platform for small and medium businesses, built with Laravel, Tailwind CSS, and Codex-assisted development workflows.</p>
      <a href="https://lavaapp.carlosmenco.site/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external-link">View app <span class="external-link-icon"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4.22876 4.22924V5.5586L9.49435 5.56332L3.75736 11.3003L4.70017 12.2431L10.4372 6.50613L10.4324 11.7717H11.7712V4.22924H4.22876Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Overview</h6>
      <p>Facturazaz is a software-as-a-service product designed to help small and medium businesses manage invoicing with a cleaner, more focused workflow.</p>
      <p>The product direction centers on reducing administrative friction: creating invoices, managing client data, tracking business activity, and giving business owners a system that feels simpler than traditional accounting software.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Role</h6>
      <p>Product concept, Laravel development, Tailwind interface implementation, application structure, workflow planning, and Codex-assisted development.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Challenge</h6>
      <p>Many invoicing tools are either too generic or too complex for small teams. The challenge was to design a SaaS foundation that could feel approachable while still supporting the operational needs of real businesses.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Solution</h6>
      <ul>
        <li>Built the application foundation with Laravel for a solid backend architecture.</li>
        <li>Used Tailwind CSS to create a clean and consistent interface system.</li>
        <li>Structured the product around practical invoicing flows for small businesses.</li>
        <li>Used Codex to accelerate implementation, improve code organization, and iterate faster on product decisions.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Outcome</h6>
      <p>Facturazaz is evolving into a focused invoicing SaaS with a clear technical foundation and a product direction aimed at making business administration easier for small companies.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
